     print("\n1. Change of Variable: \u222b[a to b] f(x)dx = \u222b[a to b] f(t)dt\n2. Interchange of Limits: \u222b[a to b] f(x)dx = - \u222b[b to a] f(x)dx\n3. Additivity / Splitting: \u222b[a to b] f(x)dx = \u222b[a to c] f(x)dx + \u222b[c to b] f(x)dx (where a < c < b)\n4. King's Property: \u222b[a to b] f(x)dx = \u222b[a to b] f(a + b - x)dx\n5. King's Special Case (0 to a): \u222b[0 to a] f(x)dx = \u222b[0 to a] f(a - x)dx\n6. Queen's Property: \u222b[0 to 2a] f(x)dx = 2\u00b7\u222b[0 to a] f(x)dx [if f(2a-x) = f(x)]\n \u222b[0 to 2a] f(x)dx = 0 [if f(2a-x) = -f(x)]\n7. Even/Odd Property: \u222b[-a to a] f(x)dx = 2\u00b7\u222b[0 to a] f(x)dx [if f(-x) = f(x) (Even)]\n \u222b[-a to a] f(x)dx = 0 [if f(-x) = -f(x) (Odd)]\n8. Periodic Property: If f(x+T) = f(x), then \u222b[0 to nT] f(x)dx = n \u00b7 \u222b[0 to T] f(x)dx (where n \u2208 Z)\n9. Periodic Shift: If f(x+T) = f(x), then \u222b[a to a+T] f(x)dx = \u222b[0 to T] f(x)dx\n10. Leibnitz Differentiation Rule: d/dx [\u222b[\u03c8(x) to \u03c6(x)] f(t)dt] = f(\u03c6(x))\u00b7\u03c6'(x) -f(\u03c8(x))\u00b7\u03c8'(x)\n11. Integral Inequality: If f(x) \u2265 g(x) on [a,b], then \u222b[a to b] f(x)dx \u2265 \u222b[a to b] g(x)dx\n12. Absolute Value Inequality: |\u222b[a to b] f(x)dx| \u2264 \u222b[a to b] |f(x)|dx\n13. Boundedness Theorem: If m \u2264 f(x) \u2264 M on [a,b], then m(b-a) \u2264 \u222b[a to b] f(x)dx \u2264 M(b-a)")
